# No AI attribution (commits and PRs)

Never add AI or tooling attribution to **commits, commit messages, PR titles, PR bodies, or PR descriptions**. `scripts/versioning` `commit-check` enforces this unconditionally on every checked surface (hook, CI `commit-lint`); it has no user-request exception, so even an explicitly requested attribution cannot land through a commit or PR — decline such requests rather than bypassing the gate.

## Scope

The ban applies to surfaces a human or agent authors. Machine-generated platform boilerplate is exempt because no authorial surface exists: PR bodies authored by bot accounts (GitHub `user.type == "Bot"` — dependabot, renovate, and similar) are generated wholesale by the platform, which injects zero-width bytes into `@`-mentions for anti-ping that this rule would otherwise flag. The exemption covers **PR bodies only**: commit messages and PR titles are scanned on every PR regardless of author type, and a bot body's content is still bound by the forbidden list when a human quotes or copies it into an authored surface.

## Forbidden (case-insensitive)

- AI `Co-Authored-By:` / `Co-authored-by:` trailers (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, ChatGPT, Codex, Gemini, or any AI/bot/`noreply` vendor address)
- Generator footers: `Generated with/by…`, `Made with…`, `Made-with:…`, `Authored via…`, `via Cursor/Claude/…`
- Bot emoji generator signatures (`🤖 Generated…`, etc.) when used as attribution
- Naming models or AI products as the **author** (allowed when they are the **subject** of the change, e.g. “add Copilot webhook”)
- First-person AI self-refs (“As an AI…”, “I generated this…”)
- HTML comments or zero-width / invisible markers used as attribution in messages

## Allowed

- Real human `Co-authored-by:` trailers
- `Signed-off-by:` for the human committer
- Normal project commit/PR conventions (Conventional Commits, issue refs, etc.)

## Pre-flight

Before `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or `gh pr create`:

1. Draft the message/body for the change only.
2. Scan subject, body, and trailers for the forbidden items above.
3. Strip any match; do not soften into alternate AI attribution. Re-scan.
4. Only then run the command.

## IDE/CLI injection

Some hosts append trailers after the agent writes the message (e.g. `Made-with: Cursor`). If `git log -1 --format=%B` shows a trailer you did not write:

1. Tell the user it came from the IDE/CLI, not the agent message.
2. Point them at Cursor **Settings → Git & PRs → Attribution** (turn off commit and PR attribution), and for CLI: `attribution.attributeCommitsToAgent` / `attribution.attributePRsToAgent` set to `false` in `~/.cursor/cli-config.json`.
3. Do **not** change those settings or rewrite files without an explicit ask.
4. Do not rewrite pushed history just to scrub old attribution; only amend unpushed commits when the user asks.
